Runtime: Events

Purpose:
  Define the runtime event architecture. Events are the historical
  record of every state change, action, policy decision, and system
  occurrence. Events are append-only and MUST NEVER be modified or
  deleted.

Principles:
  Events are immutable — history is append-only.
  Events are the source of truth for audit and debugging.
  State can be reconstructed from events.
  Event ordering is guaranteed per execution_id.

EventEnvelope:
  structure:
    event:
      id: string (unique event ID)
      type: string (event type)
      version: string (event schema version)
      timestamp: ISO 8601 with timezone
      correlation_id: string (links related events)
      causation_id: string (parent event that caused this)
      actor: string (who/what caused the event)
      source: string (system component that produced event)
      payload: object (event-specific data)

  rule: every event MUST follow this envelope
  rule: event ID is unique across all events

EventTypes:
  STATE: task or execution state changed
  STAGE: task stage changed
  GATE: gate pass/fail result
  ACTION: agent action taken
  APPROVAL: approval requested, granted, or rejected
  POLICY: policy evaluated
  TOOL: tool called or completed
  CHECKPOINT: checkpoint created
  ERROR: error occurred
  METRIC: metric recorded

EventCategories:
  DomainEvents: business-level events (UserCreated, PaymentCompleted, OrderCancelled)
  SystemEvents: execution and system-level events (ExecutionStarted, ToolCalled, ToolFailed)

EventFormat:
  minimal_event:
    2026-08-26T07:35:00+04:00 STATE EXEC-500 agent ExecutionStarted

  full_event:
    event:
      id: EVT-100
      type: STATE
      version: 1.0
      timestamp: 2026-08-26T07:35:00+04:00
      correlation_id: CORR-500
      causation_id: EVT-099
      actor: AGENT-CODER-01
      source: ExecutionEngine
      payload:
        execution_id: EXEC-500
        state_from: PENDING
        state_to: RUNNING
        reason: all prerequisites met

EventStorage:
  storage_location: .sdd/runtime/events.sdd
  format: append-only, organized by task/execution
  rule: events are stored in a single append-only structure
  rule: events are organized by task/execution

EventRetention:
  rule: events are retained indefinitely for audit
  rule: events MAY be archived to cold storage
  rule: archive MUST remain queryable
  rule: events MUST NOT be deleted or compacted

EventVersioning:
  rule: event schemas are versioned
  rule: consumers MUST handle old event versions
  rule: schema changes require migration

EventImmutability:
  rule: events cannot be modified after creation
  rule: corrections create new events, not modifications
  rule: event history is never rewritten

DuplicateEvents:
  rule: consumers MUST handle duplicate events
  rule: deduplication is by event_id
  rule: processing the same event twice MUST NOT cause side effects

DeadLetterQueue:
  rule: events that cannot be processed go to DLQ
  rule: DLQ is monitored and reprocessed
  rule: DLQ events are analyzed for systemic issues

Ordering:
  rule: ordering is guaranteed per execution_id
  rule: global ordering across executions is NOT required
  rule: ordering is implemented via partitioning

CorrelationID:
  definition: ID that links all events in a workflow
  rule: correlation_id is set at workflow start
  rule: all subsequent events inherit correlation_id

CausationID:
  definition: ID of the event that caused this event
  rule: causation_id creates causal chain
  rule: causation_id enables root cause analysis

Security:
  rule: sensitive data MUST be redacted in events
  rule: SECRET classified events are never logged in plain text
  rule: event access is controlled by policy

DataClassification:
  levels: PUBLIC, INTERNAL, CONFIDENTIAL, SECRET
  rule: all event payloads MUST be classified
  rule: SECRET data is replaced with [REDACTED]

AIReadRestriction:
  rule: AI MUST NOT read the entire events file
  rule: AI MUST filter by task ID or time range
  rule: AI MUST only read events relevant to current task

Navigation:
  Runtime: @INDEX.sdd
  Execution: @execution.sdd
  Context: @context.sdd
  Orchestrator: @../orchestrator/INDEX.sdd

Rules:
  [E1] Every state change MUST produce a STATE event.
  [E2] Every stage change MUST produce a STAGE event.
  [E3] Every gate result MUST produce a GATE event.
  [E4] Every policy evaluation MUST produce a POLICY event.
  [E5] Every tool call MUST produce a TOOL event.
  [E6] Every approval request MUST produce an APPROVAL event.
  [E7] Every checkpoint MUST produce a CHECKPOINT event.
  [E8] Every error MUST produce an ERROR event.
  [E9] Every metric MUST produce a METRIC event.
  [E10] Events are immutable and append-only.
  [E11] Event ordering is guaranteed per execution_id.
  [E12] Event consumers MUST be idempotent.
  [E13] Duplicate events MUST be handled gracefully.
  [E14] Failed events go to Dead Letter Queue.
  [E15] Sensitive data MUST be redacted in all events.
  [E16] Events MUST be classified (PUBLIC, INTERNAL, CONFIDENTIAL, SECRET).
  [E17] AI MUST NOT read the entire events file — only relevant events.
  [E18] Event schemas are versioned; consumers handle old versions.
  [E19] Correlation ID links workflow events; Causation ID links causal chain.
  [E20] Events are retained indefinitely; archive remains queryable.
  [E21] Agent MUST NOT add signatures or sign-offs to event outputs.
  [E22] Agent MUST NOT use emojis, icons, or decorative symbols in event output headers or titles.

State: +